<section class="install" data-section="install">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="install__layout">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow reveal">Installation</div>
        <h2 class="section-h reveal">Up and running before lunch.</h2>
        <p class="section-sub reveal">No contractor, no all-day project. Just a drill, a little muscle, and about an hour of your Saturday.</p>

        <ol class="steps reveal">
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">1</span>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h3>Set the post</h3>
              <p>Two ways, your call: slide it over a wooden 4x4 set in the ground, or bolt it straight to concrete through the four holes in the base.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">2</span>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h3>Mount the mailbox</h3>
              <p>Bolt the mailbox to the post with the included hardware &mdash; a drill and a wrench is all it takes.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="step-num">3</span>
            <div class="step-body">
              <h3>Snap on your numbers</h3>
              <p>The 4-inch address numbers are magnetic &mdash; press them into place, step back, and admire the new curb appeal.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <div class="tools-line reveal">
          <strong>Tools:</strong> drill, wrench, level. The 4x4 (or concrete anchors) are up to you &mdash; not included.
        </div>
        <p class="compat-note reveal">Heads up: <em>The Malone</em> ships in two boxes, mailbox and post, and they occasionally arrive a day apart. Full step-by-step instructions and the install video are at <a href="https://postandporch.com/pages/installation?utm_source=lp&amp;utm_medium=landing&amp;utm_campaign=malone-v1&amp;lp=malone-v1" target="_blank" rel="noopener">postandporch.com/installation</a>.</p>
